@@ -19,6 +19,39 @@ the changes up. Other options: `--once`, `--dry-run`, `--retries N`,
 `--timeout S`, `--manifest-path PATH`, `--allow-empty`. `./sync-cli` is a thin
 wrapper around `python3 -m sync_cli`.
 
+## Several folders at once
+
+List the folders in a JSON config file and pass `--config` instead of
+`SERVER DEST`. Every folder syncs in parallel, on its own thread and its own
+schedule, so a slow or unreachable server doesn't hold the others up.
+
+```json
+{
+  "folders": [
+    {"server": "http://127.0.0.1:8000", "dest": "demo/local-a", "name": "a"},
+    {"server": "http://127.0.0.1:8001", "dest": "demo/local-b",
+     "manifest_path": "/manifest.json"}
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+```sh
+./sync-cli --config sync.json --interval 10
+```
+
+- `server` and `dest` are required; `name` (used to prefix log lines,
+  defaults to `dest`) and `manifest_path` are optional.
+- A relative `dest` is resolved against the config file's directory.
+- Destinations must not be the same folder or nested inside each other.
+- The other options (`--interval`, `--once`, `--dry-run`, `--retries`,
+  `--timeout`, `--allow-empty`) apply to every folder.
+- Each folder takes its own lock; if any is already being synced by another
+  instance, sync-cli exits with code 2 before starting.
+- With `--once`, the exit code is 0 only if every folder synced cleanly.
+- Live progress bars are replaced by one line per file when several folders
+  share the terminal.
+- Ctrl+C lets in-flight downloads finish, then stops; press it again to force.
+
 ## What the server must provide
 
 - `GET /manifest.json` returns `{"files": [{"path": "a/b.txt", "size": 123, "sha256": "..."}]}`
